  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the following reactions, <strong>P, Q, R</strong> and <strong>S</strong> are the major products.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/3bd9e18b-3126-471e-8403-a7bcc7947e7e.png\" style=\"width: 457px; height: 349px;\" /></p><p>The correct statement(s) about <strong>P, Q, R</strong> and <strong>S</strong> is(are)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "pPSc2",
      "text": "Both <strong>P</strong> and <strong>Q</strong> have asymmetric carbon(s)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LswFz",
      "text": "Both <strong>Q</strong> and <strong>R</strong> have asymmetric carbon(s)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "BKL2z",
      "text": "Both <strong>P</strong> and <strong>R</strong> have asymmetric carbon(s)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Myjx9",
      "text": "<strong>P</strong> has asymmetric carbon(s), <strong>S</strong> does not have any asymmetric carbon",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The cyanide part undergoes reaction with phenyl magnesium bromide followed by acidic water give a ketone. The ketone undergoes reaction with phenyl magnesium bromide again to get a tertiary alcohol.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/35079bc0-a55e-42d7-86b8-a85d2f500db4.png\" style=\"width: 641px; height: 270px;\" /></p><p>Benzene undergo Friedel craft acylation and gives acetophenone. Acetophenone gives a tertiary alcohol upon reaction with phenyl magnesium bromide.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/3cabcfed-2f17-4ae7-91e6-71cb3840bddd.png\" style=\"width: 610px; height: 119px;\" /></p><p>Propanoyl chloride when treated with dibenzyl cadmium gives a ketone. The ketone give tertiary alcohol on reaction with phenyl magnesium bromide.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/ffc71cd1-3e76-47a0-a04b-783452cd6f95.png\" style=\"width: 562px; height: 254px;\" /></p><p>2-phenyl ethanal gives 1,2-diphenylethanol. The secondary&nbsp;alcohol formed gives a ketone up on reaction with Jone&#39;s reagent. The ketone formed undergo nucleophilic addition reaction with hydrogen cyanide to give cyano hydrin which undergo hydrolysis followed elimination give the final product as shown below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/331dc7fa-3ddb-4007-bd6c-a50fd65b64a7.png\" style=\"width: 628px; height: 212px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
